Offer a removed library root back only while a file under it is on disk.

Why: Settings > Library shows "Library roots were removed ... Restore it to
keep your library working without a rescan" for every root id the catalog
still holds rows for. A root whose files were all moved away keeps its rows
as `missing`, so the banner offers to restore a folder that no longer
exists, with nothing it could bring back. Measured 2026-10-25 on
music.xarif.de: root `seafile` (/data/music-seafile, gone since its files
were moved into /data/music on 2026-10-24) is offered with
indexed_file_count 2483, and all 2,483 of its rows are `missing`; restoring
it would only add a root at a missing path. The catalog read behind the
offer and the restore now leaves out a root none of whose rows is still on
disk (`indexed` or `excluded`). The count of an offered root is unchanged
(every row, as v2 counted and the existing test pins).

Tests: new integration test (a removed root with every file missing is not
offered, and a restore finds nothing to restore). It fails without the
change. Library integration suite (symlink-free TMPDIR): same 5 failures
with and without the patch.

Remove when: upstream stops offering roots with no file left on disk.

